  "summary": [
    "Pre-search check distinguishes rebuild-not-needed, rebuild-needed and undeterminable states; undeterminable stops search as a failure.",
    "When a rebuild is needed, the Skill asks the user to choose rebuild-then-search or search the existing version, showing rebuild scale counts.",
    "Details go to work files under .temp/doc-link/query-docs/, including a target-specification file passed via --target-file.",
    "Each search candidate carries document ID, recorded path, reason, optional sections, ToC key, version and freshness.",
    "The search AI reads every entry of a fixed ToC copy and favors recall, selecting any document that might be relevant.",
    "The ToC copy holds titles, purposes, summaries, tasks, keywords and section headings, but no paths, hashes or references.",
    "The script validates returned IDs against the fixed ToC version, drops invalid or duplicate IDs, reports them, and fails if all are invalid.",
    "resolve-dlid resolves each DLID from recorded paths by checking the actual file frontmatter or heading suffix, returning content hashes.",
    "Unresolvable DLIDs return not-at-recorded-path or no-record; no other locations are searched and nothing is written."
  ],
